For the BibleHub URL: `https://biblehub.com/greek/${(w.s||'').replace('G','')}.htm`
If w.s is "H7225", the `.replace('G','')` won't do anything, producing `https://biblehub.com/greek/H7225.htm` which is wrong.

But wait, for WLC morphology, the Strong's is stored as `H{number}` in the ingest code. So `w.s` would be "H7225". The `.replace('G','')` won't strip the H, so it'd be `https://biblehub.com/greek/H7225.htm` — that's broken for Hebrew.

The correct BibleHub URL for Hebrew would be: `https://biblehub.com/hebrew/7225.htm`

So the findings claim about BLB URL differences is PARTIALLY correct — BLB handles it fine (both /tr/ and /wlc/ work), but BibleHub is genuinely broken because:
1. Path uses `/greek/` instead of `/hebrew/`
2. The `.replace('G','')` doesn't strip the `H` prefix

This is a confirmed bug.
